# Java Semester Programs

## 📌 Overview

This repository contains a collection of Java programs developed as part of my semester coursework.
The programs are designed to demonstrate fundamental and intermediate concepts in Java programming.

## 🎯 Objectives

* Strengthen understanding of core Java concepts
* Practice problem-solving using Java
* Build a solid foundation in object-oriented programming
* Prepare for academic exams and practical assessments

## 🧠 Topics Covered

* Arrays and Strings
* Object-Oriented Programming (OOP)
* File Handling
* Exception Handling
* Collections Framework
* Basic Mini Projects

## 📂 Folder Structure

Each folder contains programs related to a specific topic:

* `Program-01-Arrays` → Array-based problems
* `Program-02-Strings` → String manipulation programs
* `Program-03-OOP` → Classes, objects, inheritance, polymorphism
* `Program-04-File-Handling` → Reading and writing files
* `Program-05-Exception-Handling` → Error handling techniques
* `Program-06-Collections` → List, Set, Map implementations
* `Program-07-Mini-Projects` → Small practical applications

## 🛠 Technologies Used

* Java (JDK 8 or above)
* IDE: IntelliJ IDEA / Eclipse / VS Code

## 👨‍💻 Author

PROSPERITY
Computer Science Student

## 📌 Note

These programs are created for academic learning purposes and may be improved over time as I continue to learn and grow in Java development.

